- Story & Context: According to rail yard myth, the ghost of night-switchman Silas still trips the frozen track levers at Siding Nine, where the EP's final recordings were captured directly off an abandoned telegraph wire during a blizzard. Devon layered Silas’s rhythmic signal-box clicks through an aggressive 16-step pocket sequencer, letting Clara's contrabassoon generate a crushing, subsonic groove that made the ice on the rails crack in 4/4 time. As dawn broke over the rusted switches, the track dissolved into a multi-tracked choir of ghostly falsetto harmonies layered over dying 8-bit blips and down-tuned acoustic picking. "No return address when the rails take your name!"
